{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "```python\ndef differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the binary representations of two integers differ at exactly one bit position.\n    \"\"\"\n    xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n\n    set_bits_count = 0\n    # Counts the number of set bits (1s) in xor_result using Brian Kernighan's algorithm.\n    while xor_result > 0:\n        xor_result &= (xor_result - 1)\n        set_bits_count += 1\n\n    return set_bits_count == 1\n```"}
