{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _calculate_row_sum(row: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a given row.\"\"\"\n    return sum(row)\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    It uses a helper function to calculate row sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = _calculate_row_sum(row)\n        rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda item: item[0])\n\n    sorted_matrix = [row for row_sum, row in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    If the character appears less than twice, the original string is returned.\"\"\"\n    char_count = input_string.count(char_to_remove)\n\n    if char_count < 2:\n        return input_string\n    else:\n        first_index = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n        last_index = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n        # Remove the first occurrence of the character\n        temp_string = input_string[:first_index] + input_string[first_index+1:]\n\n        # Adjust last_index as the removal of the first character shifts subsequent indices\n        # Since first_index is always less than or equal to last_index for distinct occurrences,\n        # the effective index of the last character in temp_string will be last_index - 1.\n        adjusted_last_index = last_index - 1\n\n        # Remove the second (now adjusted) occurrence of the character\n        modified_string = temp_string[:adjusted_last_index] + temp_string[adjusted_last_index+1:]\n\n        return modified_string\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    Preserves the order of other characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:]\n    else:\n        intermediate_string = input_string[:last_idx] + input_string[last_idx+1:]\n        return intermediate_string[:first_idx] + intermediate_string[first_idx+1:]\n```"}
