{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_number(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the digits of a non-negative integer.\n    For example, _reverse_number(123) returns 321.\n    \"\"\"\n    reversed_num = 0\n    original_num = num\n    while original_num > 0:\n        digit = original_num % 10\n        reversed_num = reversed_num * 10 + digit\n        original_num //= 10\n    return reversed_num\n\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    It utilizes a helper function to determine the reversed number.\n    \"\"\"\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number(num)\n    return num == (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n```"}
