{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_sum_of_digits(substring_val: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of integer digits in a string.\n    Each character is converted to an integer and added to the total.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for char_digit in substring_val:\n        total_sum += int(char_digit)\n    return total_sum\n\ndef _get_length(substring_val: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the length of the given string.\n    This uses Python's built-in len() function.\n    \"\"\"\n    return len(substring_val)\n\ndef count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    It iterates through all possible substrings, calculates their sum of digits and length,\n    and increments a counter if they are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            substring = s[i : j + 1]\n            sum_of_digits = _calculate_sum_of_digits(substring)\n            length = _get_length(substring)\n\n            if sum_of_digits == length:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```\n"}
