{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "```python\nclass Pair:\n    \"\"\"Represents a pair of numerical values.\n    It calculates their absolute difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, val1: float, val2: float):\n        self.value1 = float(val1)\n        self.value2 = float(val2)\n\n    def getDifference(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the absolute difference between value1 and value2.\"\"\"\n        return abs(self.value1 - self.value2)\n\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: list[tuple[float, float]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum absolute difference between pairs in the given tuple list.\n    Returns 0.0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0.0\n\n    max_diff = 0.0\n    for item in tuple_list:\n        pair = Pair(item[0], item[1])\n        current_diff = pair.getDifference()\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n\n    return max_diff\n```"}
