{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n-th Bell number, which represents the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    This implementation uses Stirling numbers of the second kind for computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # S[i][j] stores the Stirling number of the second kind S(i, j)\n    # S(i, j) is the number of ways to partition a set of i elements into j non-empty subsets.\n    S = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers: S(0, 0) = 1\n    S[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for Stirling numbers of the second kind\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            S[i][j] = S[i - 1][j - 1] + j * S[i - 1][j]\n\n    # The n-th Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n\n    bell_n = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += S[n][k]\n\n    return bell_n\n```"}
