{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n-th Bell number using dynamic programming and a Bell triangle.\n    It determines the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D array for the Bell triangle.\n    bell = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Set the base case for the triangle.\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Populate the Bell triangle using recurrence relations.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i][j-1] + bell[i-1][j-1]\n\n    # The n-th Bell number is the first element of the n-th row.\n    return bell[n][0]\n```"}
