{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new list with the elements sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    arr = list(numbers)  # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr\n```"}
