{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(words: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of words follows a given pattern sequence based on a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Returns True if the mapping is consistent, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(words) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    word_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_word_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        current_word = words[i]\n        current_pattern = patterns[i]\n\n        if current_word in word_to_pattern_map:\n            if word_to_pattern_map[current_word] != current_pattern:\n                return False\n        elif current_pattern in pattern_to_word_map:\n            if pattern_to_word_map[current_pattern] != current_word:\n                return False\n        else:\n            word_to_pattern_map[current_word] = current_pattern\n            pattern_to_word_map[current_pattern] = current_word\n\n    return True\n```"}
