{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef is_samepatterns(strings: List[Any], patterns: List[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of strings follows a given pattern sequence, establishing a one-to-one mapping.\n    Ensures consistent bidirectional mapping for repeating elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(strings) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_string_map = {}\n    string_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(strings)):\n        current_string = strings[i]\n        current_pattern = patterns[i]\n\n        if current_pattern in pattern_to_string_map:\n            # If the pattern is already mapped, ensure its existing mapping matches the current string.\n            if pattern_to_string_map[current_pattern] != current_string:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If the pattern is new, check if the current string is already mapped to a different pattern.\n            if current_string in string_to_pattern_map:\n                if string_to_pattern_map[current_string] != current_pattern:\n                    return False\n            # If both are new or consistently related, establish the new bidirectional mapping.\n            pattern_to_string_map[current_pattern] = current_string\n            string_to_pattern_map[current_string] = current_pattern\n\n    return True\n```"}
