{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Diff(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    Returns True if the absolute difference between sums of digits at odd and even places is divisible by 11, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(abs(number))\n    sum_odd_places = 0\n    sum_even_places = 0\n\n    # Iterate through the digits from right to left,\n    # treating the rightmost digit as being at the 1st (odd) place.\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(reversed(num_str)):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if (i + 1) % 2 == 1:  # 1st, 3rd, 5th, ... positions from the right\n            sum_odd_places += digit\n        else:  # 2nd, 4th, 6th, ... positions from the right\n            sum_even_places += digit\n\n    difference = abs(sum_odd_places - sum_even_places)\n    return difference % 11 == 0\n```"}
