{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(elements: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with the elements sorted, leaving the original unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(elements)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(elements)\n\n    current_list = list(elements)  # Create a mutable copy of the input list\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1  # Ensure gap is at least 1 for the final pass\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if current_list[i] > current_list[i + gap]:\n                current_list[i], current_list[i + gap] = current_list[i + gap], current_list[i]\n                swapped = True\n\n    return current_list\n```"}
