{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\ndef divisor(integer_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of positive divisors for a given integer.\n    It efficiently counts divisors by iterating up to the square root of the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= integer_value:\n        if integer_value % i == 0:\n            if i * i == integer_value:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n        i += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "import math\n\ndef divisor(integer_value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total count of positive divisors for a given integer.\n    It expects a positive integer input.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of the number to find divisors efficiently.\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(integer_value)) + 1):\n        if integer_value % i == 0:\n            if i * i == integer_value:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n    return count"}
