{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal_number: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n    Ensures no leading zeros, handling the special case of 0.\"\"\"\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    num = decimal_number\n    while num > 0:\n        remainder = num % 2\n        binary_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        num //= 2\n\n    return \"\".join(binary_digits[::-1])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(decimal_number: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n    The output string will not have leading zeros, except for the input 0 which returns \"0\".\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    # Python's built-in bin() function returns a string prefixed with \"0b\".\n    # Slicing from index 2 removes this prefix to fulfill the no-leading-zeros requirement.\n    return bin(decimal_number)[2:]\n```"}
