{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef index_minimum(data: List[Tuple[Any, Any]]) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list of tuples, returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains at least two elements.\n              The second element of each tuple must be comparable.\n\n    Returns:\n        The first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input is not a list, is empty, or contains invalid tuple elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_value = None\n    result = None\n\n    for item in data:\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple) or len(item) < 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each element in the list must be a tuple with at least two elements.\")\n\n        current_second_value = item[1]\n        current_first_value = item[0]\n\n        if min_value is None or current_second_value < min_value:\n            min_value = current_second_value\n            result = current_first_value\n\n    return result\n```"}
