{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of odd decimal equivalents from binary string rotations.\"\"\"\n\n    def _rotate_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs a single left cyclic rotation on a string.\"\"\"\n        if not s:\n            return s\n        return s[1:] + s[0]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(s: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n        return int(s, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if an integer is odd.\"\"\"\n        return n % 2 != 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n\n    for i in range(num_rotations):\n        if i > 0:\n            current_string = _rotate_string(current_string)\n\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(current_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns elements present in all sub-lists within a given nested list.\n    Leverages set intersections for efficient computation of common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    common_set = set(list_of_lists[0])\n\n    for sub_list in list_of_lists[1:]:\n        common_set.intersection_update(set(sub_list))\n        if not common_set:  # Early exit if no common elements are found\n            break\n\n    return common_set\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all sublists within a given list of lists.\n    Returns a set containing these common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Start with the elements of the first list as the initial common set\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the lists and find intersections\n    for current_list in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(set(current_list))\n\n    return common_elements\n```"}
