{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts how many of n left rotations of a binary string result in an odd decimal number.\n    An odd decimal number is defined by its least significant bit (rightmost character) being '1'.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    string_length = len(binary_string)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        idx = (string_length - 1 + i) % string_length\n        if binary_string[idx] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
