{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number.\n    Proper divisors are all positive divisors excluding the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, int(n**0.5) + 1): # Optimized loop up to sqrt(n)\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i != n: # Exclude n itself\n                total_sum += i\n            if i * i != n and i != 1: # Add the other divisor if not a perfect square root and not 1 (already added)\n                total_sum += n // i\n    return total_sum\n\ndef is_amicable_pair(a: int, b: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if two numbers form an amicable pair.\n    An amicable pair (a, b) consists of two different numbers\n    such that the sum of proper divisors of a is b and vice versa.\n    \"\"\"\n    return a != b and sum_proper_divisors(a) == b and sum_proper_divisors(b) == a\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(upper_limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to a specified upper limit.\n    It identifies amicable pairs and sums their unique members.\n    \"\"\"\n    amicable_numbers_found = set()\n    total_amicable_sum = 0\n\n    for n in range(1, upper_limit + 1):\n        if n in amicable_numbers_found:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_n = sum_proper_divisors(n)\n\n        if sum_div_n > n and sum_div_n <= upper_limit and is_amicable_pair(n, sum_div_n):\n            total_amicable_sum += n\n            total_amicable_sum += sum_div_n\n            amicable_numbers_found.add(n)\n            amicable_numbers_found.add(sum_div_n)\n\n    return total_amicable_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum difference between '0's and '1's in any substring using Kadane's algorithm.\"\"\"\n    max_diff = 0\n    current_max = 0\n    for char in binary_string:\n        val = 1 if char == '0' else -1\n        current_max += val\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        max_diff = max(max_diff, current_max)\n    return max_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_of_common_divisors(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two integers a and b.\n    Returns the sum of their common divisors.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    limit = min(abs(a), abs(b)) + 1\n\n    for i in range(1, limit):\n        if a % i == 0 and b % i == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
