{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two integers.\n    It uses the greatest common divisor to find all common divisors efficiently.\"\"\"\n\n    # Compute the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the two numbers.\n    # All common divisors of num1 and num2 are also divisors of their GCD.\n    gcd_val = math.gcd(num1, num2)\n\n    sum_of_divs = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of GCD to find all its divisors and sum them.\n    # This optimization prevents iterating all the way up to GCD_val.\n    for i in range(1, int(gcd_val**0.5) + 1):\n        if gcd_val % i == 0:\n            sum_of_divs += i\n            if i * i != gcd_val: # If i is not the square root, add its pair divisor\n                sum_of_divs += gcd_val // i\n\n    return sum_of_divs\n```"}
