{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "```python\ndef kth_element(array: list, k: int) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th element in the given array using 1-based indexing.\n\n    Args:\n        array: The input list/array.\n        k: The 1-based index of the element to retrieve.\n\n    Returns:\n        The element at the k-th position.\n\n    Raises:\n        IndexError: If k is out of bounds (1 <= k <= len(array)).\n        TypeError: If array is not a list or k is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(array, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'array' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'k' must be an integer.\")\n    if not array:\n        raise IndexError(\"Cannot find element in an empty array.\")\n    if not (1 <= k <= len(array)):\n        raise IndexError(f\"k ({k}) is out of bounds for array of length {len(array)}. Must be between 1 and {len(array)} (inclusive).\")\n\n    # Convert 1-based index to 0-based index\n    zero_based_index = k - 1\n    return array[zero_based_index]\n```"}
