{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and number of 1s in any sub-string\n    of the given binary string.\n    This uses a variant of Kadane's algorithm by transforming '0's to 1 and '1's to -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    # Transform '0' to 1 and '1' to -1 to apply Kadane's algorithm.\n    # We are looking for max(count_0s - count_1s).\n    # If '0' becomes 1 and '1' becomes -1, then the sum of transformed array elements\n    # directly gives (count_0s - count_1s).\n    transformed_array = [1 if char == '0' else -1 for char in binary_string]\n\n    current_max_sum = transformed_array[0]\n    global_max_sum = transformed_array[0]\n\n    for num in transformed_array[1:]:\n        current_max_sum = max(num, current_max_sum + num)\n        global_max_sum = max(global_max_sum, current_max_sum)\n\n    return global_max_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number can be represented as the sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This excludes 2^0 (which is 1).\n\n    Args:\n        number (int): The integer to check.\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if the number can be represented as the sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2,\n              False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2 must be positive and even.\n    # If the number is odd or non-positive, it cannot be such a sum.\n    if number <= 0 or number % 2 != 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Any positive even number can be uniquely represented as a sum of distinct powers of 2,\n    # and none of these will be 2^0 because the number is even.\n    return True\n```"}
