{"task_id": "Mbpp/139", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input parameters for geometric calculations.\n    Ensures radius is a non-negative numerical value.\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate_radius(self, radius: any) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the radius is a non-negative numerical value.\n        Raises ValueError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"Radius must be a numerical value.\")\n        if radius < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Radius cannot be negative.\")\n        return float(radius)\n\nclass CircleCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates geometric properties of a circle.\n    Uses InputValidator for validation and a high-precision PI.\n    \"\"\"\n    PI: float = math.pi # High-precision value for Pi (\u03c0).\n\n    def __init__(self, validator: InputValidator):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the calculator with an InputValidator instance.\"\"\"\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def circle_circumference(self, radius: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the circumference of a circle given its radius.\n        Delegates input validation and uses the internal PI.\n        \"\"\"\n        validated_radius = self._validator.validate_radius(radius)\n        return 2 * self.PI * validated_radius\n\n# Instantiate components as singletons for the global entry point.\n_input_validator_instance = InputValidator()\n_circle_calculator_instance = CircleCalculator(validator=_input_validator_instance)\n\ndef circle_circumference(radius: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the circumference of a circle.\n    This is the public entry point, leveraging the CircleCalculator component.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _circle_calculator_instance.circle_circumference(radius)\n```"}
