{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    sorted_list = list(input_list) # Create a mutable copy of the input list.\n\n    # Iterate from the largest element's position down to the second element.\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted prefix.\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, current_size):\n            if sorted_list[i] > sorted_list[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # If the largest element is not already at the end of the current prefix, perform flips.\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # First flip: bring the largest element from max_idx to the front.\n            sorted_list[:max_idx + 1] = sorted_list[:max_idx + 1][::-1]\n\n            # Second flip: move the largest element from the front to its sorted position.\n            sorted_list[:current_size] = sorted_list[:current_size][::-1]\n\n    return sorted_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef _flip(arr: List[int], i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reverses elements in a list from index 0 up to index i (inclusive) in-place.\"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    end = i\n    while start < end:\n        arr[start], arr[end] = arr[end], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        end -= 1\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr: List[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements of a list.\"\"\"\n    max_idx = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        if arr[j] > arr[max_idx]:\n            max_idx = j\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the pancake sorting algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    working_list = list(arr)  # Create a shallow copy to ensure immutability\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted sublist\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(working_list, current_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct sorted position\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Bring the maximum element to the front if it's not already there\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                _flip(working_list, max_idx)\n            # Bring the maximum element from the front to its sorted position\n            _flip(working_list, current_size - 1)\n\n    return working_list"}
