{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    def egcd(a_val, b_val):\n        \"\"\"Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find gcd(a, b) and coefficients x, y.\"\"\"\n        if a_val == 0:\n            return (b_val, 0, 1)\n        else:\n            g, x, y = egcd(b_val % a_val, a_val)\n            return (g, y - (b_val // a_val) * x, x)\n\n    # Handle the special case where both a and b are zero\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    # Use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find gcd(a, b) and coefficients\n    g, x_g, y_g = egcd(a, b)\n\n    # If n is not divisible by gcd(a, b), no integer solution exists\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Calculate the scaling factor and the particular solution\n    k = n // g\n    x = x_g * k\n    y = y_g * k\n\n    return (x, y)\n```"}
