{"task_id": "Mbpp/162", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_series(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the series n + (n-2) + (n-4) + ...\n    where each term is strictly greater than 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_term = n\n    total_sum = 0\n    while current_term > 0:\n        total_sum += current_term\n        current_term -= 2\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two integers and their Bezout coefficients.\n    Returns (g, x, y) such that ax + by = g, where g is gcd(a, b).\"\"\"\n    if b == 0:\n        return (a, 1, 0)\n    g_rec, x_prime_rec, y_prime_rec = _extended_gcd(b, a % b)\n    x_curr = y_prime_rec\n    y_curr = x_prime_rec - (a // b) * y_prime_rec\n    return (g_rec, x_curr, y_curr)\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\"\"\"\n    g, x_prime, y_prime = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n\n    factor = n // g\n    x = x_prime * factor\n    y = y_prime * factor\n    return (x, y)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/162", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_series(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the series (n - 2*i) for i from 0 to n // 2.\n    It sums terms like n, (n-2), (n-4), and so on, until the term is 0 or less.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # The loop goes from i=0 up to and including n // 2\n    for i in range((n // 2) + 1):\n        term = n - (2 * i)\n        total_sum += term\n    return total_sum\n```"}
