{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_parity(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer is even or odd.\n    Returns 0 for even, 1 for odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2\n\n\ndef find_even_pair(list_of_integers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list whose bitwise XOR sum is an even number.\n    This occurs when both integers have the same parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_pair_count = 0\n    n = len(list_of_integers)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = list_of_integers[i]\n            num2 = list_of_integers[j]\n\n            # The XOR sum of two numbers is even if their parities are the same.\n            if _get_parity(num1) == _get_parity(num2):\n                even_pair_count += 1\n\n    return even_pair_count\n```"}
