{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list, n: int, element: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element is a majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _bisect_left(a, x, lo, hi):\n        \"\"\"Return the index where to insert item x in list a, assuming a is sorted.\n        The return value i is such that all e in a[:i] have e < x, and all e in a[i:] have e >= x.\"\"\"\n        while lo < hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if a[mid] < x:\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid\n        return lo\n\n    def _bisect_right(a, x, lo, hi):\n        \"\"\"Return the index where to insert item x in list a, assuming a is sorted.\n        The return value i is such that all e in a[:i] have e <= x, and all e in a[i:] have e > x.\"\"\"\n        while lo < hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if x < a[mid]:\n                hi = mid\n            else:\n                lo = mid + 1\n        return lo\n\n    first_idx = _bisect_left(arr, element, 0, n)\n\n    if first_idx >= n or arr[first_idx] != element:\n        return False\n\n    rightmost_insertion_point = _bisect_right(arr, element, 0, n)\n\n    count = rightmost_insertion_point - first_idx\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
