{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef _find_first_occurrence(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first index of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_idx = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an even earlier occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_idx\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last index of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    last_idx = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_idx = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find an even later occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_idx\n\ndef is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given element is a majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, n, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n    return count > n / 2\n```"}
