{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits (0-indexed from the right) of the input number to 1.\n    This adheres to the general rule of setting bits, resolving design conflict.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_bits_mask = 0\n    # Iterates up to the number of bits required to represent 'number' (its bit_length).\n    # This dynamically scopes the mask to the magnitude of the input integer.\n    for i in range(number.bit_length()):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # If the bit index is even\n            even_bits_mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Performs a bitwise OR operation to set all even bits of the input 'number' to 1.\n    return number | even_bits_mask\n```"}
