{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(array)\n    lis_sum = [0] * n  # Stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[i].\n    lds_sum = [0] * n  # Stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at array[i].\n\n    # Populate lis_sum\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis_sum[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], array[i] + lis_sum[j])\n\n    # Populate lds_sum\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        lds_sum[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], array[i] + lds_sum[j])\n\n    # Calculate max bitonic sum by combining LIS and LDS sums\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Subtract array[i] to avoid double counting the peak element.\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - array[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def _calculate_lis_sums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index.\n    Returns a list where lis_sums[i] is the max sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    lis_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], arr[i] + lis_sums[j])\n    return lis_sums\n\ndef _calculate_lds_sums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each index.\n    Returns a list where lds_sums[i] is the max sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    lds_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], arr[i] + lds_sums[j])\n    return lds_sums\n\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in an array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    lis_sums = _calculate_lis_sums(arr)\n    lds_sums = _calculate_lds_sums(arr)\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Subtract arr[i] as it is counted in both LIS and LDS sums as the peak.\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\n    It builds a DP table where dp[i][j] stores the LPS length for the substring s[i...j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for substring input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                if length == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence.\n    This uses a dynamic programming approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Build the table. cl is current length of substring\n    for cl in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - cl + 1):\n            j = i + cl - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j] and cl == 2:\n                dp[i][j] = 2\n            elif input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j])\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
