{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is prime.\n    This helper function is used by count_Primes_nums.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of num.\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True\n\n\ndef count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    It iterates from 2 up to n-1 and uses _is_prime to check each number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    # Iterate for numbers strictly less than n, starting from 2.\n    for number in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(number):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count\n```\n"}
