{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "```python\n# Helper function to check if a number is prime.\n# Uses trial division up to the square root of the number.\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True\n\n# Helper function to generate the k-th term of the NSW sequence.\n# The sequence is defined by S_0 = 1, S_1 = 1, and S_k = 2S_{k-1} + S_{k-2}.\ndef _generate_nsw_sequence_term(k: int) -> int:\n    if k == 0:\n        return 1\n    if k == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    s_prev2 = 1\n    s_prev1 = 1\n\n    for _ in range(2, k + 1):\n        s_current = 2 * s_prev1 + s_prev2\n        s_prev2 = s_prev1\n        s_prev1 = s_current\n    return s_prev1\n\n# Main function to find the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number.\n# It iterates through NSW terms, checking primality until the nth prime is found.\ndef newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    prime_count = 0\n    m = 0\n    current_nsw_prime = None\n\n    while prime_count < n:\n        nsw_term = _generate_nsw_sequence_term(m)\n        if _is_prime(nsw_term):\n            prime_count += 1\n            current_nsw_prime = nsw_term\n        m += 1\n\n    return current_nsw_prime\n```\n"}
