{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "```python\ndef dog_age(human_age: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in 'dog years' based on a human age.\n    The first two human years count as 10.5 dog years each, and subsequent years count as 4 dog years each.\n    \"\"\"\n    if human_age <= 2:\n        return human_age * 10.5\n    else:\n        # Calculate dog years for the initial two human years.\n        first_two_years_dog_age = 2 * 10.5\n        # Calculate dog years for remaining human years.\n        remaining_human_years = human_age - 2\n        remaining_years_dog_age = remaining_human_years * 4\n        return first_two_years_dog_age + remaining_years_dog_age\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "```python\ndef list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list into n sublists based on an nth element pattern.\n    Elements are distributed cyclically, preserving their original order within sublists.\"\"\"\n\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    if not input_list:\n        return result\n\n    for index, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result[index % n].append(item)\n\n    return result\n```"}
