{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef _kadane(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum contiguous subarray sum using Kadane's algorithm.\n    It correctly handles cases where all numbers in the array are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_current = arr[0]\n    max_global = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        max_current = max(arr[i], max_current + arr[i])\n        max_global = max(max_global, max_current)\n\n    return max_global\n\ndef _max_prefix_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum prefix sum of the array.\n    This function tracks the largest sum encountered starting from the beginning.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    max_pref = -math.inf\n\n    for num in arr:\n        current_sum += num\n        max_pref = max(max_pref, current_sum)\n    return max_pref\n\ndef _max_suffix_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum suffix sum of the array.\n    This function finds the largest sum encountered ending at the array's end.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    max_suff = -math.inf\n\n    for num in reversed(arr):\n        current_sum += num\n        max_suff = max(max_suff, current_sum)\n    return max_suff\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    This uses Kadane's algorithm combined with prefix/suffix sums for repeated arrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0 # Per \"trust inputs\", assume non-empty. Returning 0 for empty array.\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return _kadane(arr)\n    else:\n        max_sum_single_array = _kadane(arr)\n        max_pref = _max_prefix_sum(arr)\n        max_suff = _max_suffix_sum(arr)\n        total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n        # Max sum can span across two concatenations (e.g., suffix of first + prefix of second)\n        max_sum_across_two_arrays = max_suff + max_pref\n\n        final_max_sum = max(max_sum_single_array, max_sum_across_two_arrays)\n\n        # If total sum is positive, it's beneficial to add full arrays in the middle\n        if total_sum > 0:\n            max_sum_repeated = max_suff + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_pref\n            final_max_sum = max(final_max_sum, max_sum_repeated)\n\n        return final_max_sum\n```"}
