{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr: list[Union[int, float]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array of numbers using a brute-force approach.\n    An inversion is a pair of indices (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    inversion_count = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                inversion_count += 1\n    return inversion_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(data_list):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum aggregate score for names from a list of (name, score) tuples.\n    It first sums scores for each name, then identifies the name with the highest total score.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregates = {}\n    for name, score in data_list:\n        aggregates[name] = aggregates.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    # Find the (name, total_score) pair with the highest aggregate score.\n    # The key function extracts the score for comparison.\n    return max(aggregates.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n```"}
