{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "def _word_starts_with_p(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a word starts with 'p' or 'P'.\"\"\"\n    return word.lower().startswith('p')\n\ndef start_withp(input_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first two words starting with 'p' (case-insensitive) from a list of strings.\"\"\"\n    p_words_found = []\n    for s in input_list:\n        words = s.split()\n        for word in words:\n            if _word_starts_with_p(word):\n                p_words_found.append(word)\n                if len(p_words_found) == 2:\n                    return tuple(p_words_found)\n    return tuple(p_words_found) # Fallback if fewer than 2 words are found (though spec implies 2 will always be found)."}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_p_word(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a word starts with 'p' or 'P', case-insensitively.\"\"\"\n    return len(word) > 0 and word[0].lower() == 'p'\n\ndef _extract_words_from_string(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a string into individual words using whitespace as a delimiter.\"\"\"\n    return text.split()\n\ndef start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the first two words starting with 'p' or 'P' from a list of strings.\n    Returns a tuple containing the words found, or None if fewer than two are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    collected_p_words = []\n\n    for current_string in word_list:\n        list_of_words = _extract_words_from_string(current_string)\n        for current_word in list_of_words:\n            if _is_p_word(current_word):\n                collected_p_words.append(current_word)\n                if len(collected_p_words) == 2:\n                    break # Two words found, exit inner loop\n        if len(collected_p_words) == 2:\n            break # Two words found, exit outer loop\n\n    # Format the output as a tuple, filling with None if words are missing.\n    first_p_word = collected_p_words[0] if len(collected_p_words) > 0 else None\n    second_p_word = collected_p_words[1] if len(collected_p_words) > 1 else None\n\n    return (first_p_word, second_p_word)\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef find_max_sum_increasing_subsequence_with_kth_element(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i] that ends with arr[k].\n    If no valid prefix subsequence exists, it returns arr[k].\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Initialize dp array: dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j].\n    dp = [arr[j] for j in range(i + 1)]\n\n    # Dynamic Programming Calculation for subsequences in arr[0...i]\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        for p in range(j):\n            if arr[p] < arr[j]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[p] + arr[j])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp where arr[j] < arr[k]\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[j])\n\n    # Calculate the final sum or handle the edge case\n    if max_prefix_sum == 0:\n        return arr[k]\n    else:\n        return max_prefix_sum + arr[k]\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], size: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix\n    until index i (inclusive) and also including the element at index k,\n    where k > i.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j] for j <= i.\n    max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Populate dp array for prefix sums.\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev_j in range(j):\n            if arr[j] > arr[prev_j]:\n                max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx[j] = max(\n                    max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx[j],\n                    max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx[prev_j] + arr[j]\n                )\n\n    # Initialize overall_max_sum with arr[k], representing the subsequence containing only arr[k].\n    overall_max_sum = arr[k]\n\n    # Iterate through prefix sums and combine with arr[k] if arr[j] can precede arr[k].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            overall_max_sum = max(overall_max_sum, max_sum_ending_at_prefix_idx[j] + arr[k])\n\n    return overall_max_sum\n\n```\n"}
