{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_all_products(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Calculates all possible products by taking one number from each list.\n    It iterates through both lists to form every possible product pair.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n    for num1 in list1:\n        for num2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(num1 * num2)\n    return all_products\n\ndef _find_k_largest(products: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts products in descending order and returns the first k elements.\n    This efficiently finds the k largest products from the given list.\n    \"\"\"\n    products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return products[:k]\n\ndef large_product(list1: list, list2: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the k largest products formed by selecting one factor from each of two given lists.\n    It orchestrates product calculation and selection of the top k products.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = _calculate_all_products(list1, list2)\n    k_largest_products = _find_k_largest(all_products, k)\n    return k_largest_products\n```"}
