{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the left-most unset bit in an integer's binary representation to 1.\n    For example, for input 10 (binary 1010), it returns 14 (binary 1110).\"\"\"\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the MSB position down to 0 to find the first unset bit.\n    for k in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (number >> k) & 1:\n            return number | (1 << k)\n\n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are set, set the next higher bit.\n    return number | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef max_aggregate(data: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> Tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Aggregates scores for each unique name and finds the name with the maximum total aggregated score.\n    Returns the name and their maximum aggregated score, or ('', 0) if the input is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return ('', 0)\n\n    aggregated_scores = defaultdict(int)\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] += score\n\n    max_name = ''\n    max_score = -1\n\n    for name, total_score in aggregated_scores.items():\n        if total_score > max_score:\n            max_score = total_score\n            max_name = name\n\n    return (max_name, max_score)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the left-most unset bit (0) in a positive integer to 1.\n    If all significant bits are set, the original integer is returned.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the bit at position i is unset (0)\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            # If unset, set it by OR-ing with a bitmask and return.\n            return n | (1 << i)\n\n    # If the loop completes, all significant bits are already set.\n    return n\n```"}
