{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\nclass MemoizationCache:\n    \"\"\"Manages the storage and retrieval of previously computed (n, max_sum) pairs.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._store: dict[int, int] = {}\n\n    def get(self, n: int) -> int | None:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the cached sum for n if present; otherwise, returns None.\"\"\"\n        return self._store.get(n)\n\n    def put(self, n: int, sum: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores the computed sum for n in the cache.\"\"\"\n        self._store[n] = sum\n\n# Module-level instance of the memoization cache\n_memo_cache = MemoizationCache()\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given integer n using the equation:\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses integer division and memoization for performance optimization.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Base case: f(0) = 0\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Check cache for pre-computed result\n    cached_result = _memo_cache.get(n)\n    if cached_result is not None:\n        return cached_result\n\n    # Recursive calculation\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    # Determine the maximum sum\n    max_sum = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n\n    # Store result in cache\n    _memo_cache.put(n, max_sum)\n\n    return max_sum\n```"}
