{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum for n using the recursive equation\n    f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n), with memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _f(k: int) -> int:\n        # Base case: For k=0 or negative, the sum is 0.\n        # This also serves as the termination condition for the recursion.\n        if k <= 0:\n            return 0\n\n        # Memoization check: If the result for k is already computed, return it.\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Recursive step: Calculate the sum of parts using integer division.\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            _f(k // 2) +\n            _f(k // 3) +\n            _f(k // 4) +\n            _f(k // 5)\n        )\n\n        # Determine the maximum between the sum of parts and k itself.\n        result = max(sum_of_parts, k)\n\n        # Store the computed result in the memoization dictionary before returning.\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _f(n)\n```"}
