{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(array_of_integers: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a pair of integers from the given array that yields the highest product.\n    The function handles both positive and negative numbers to find the maximum product.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_array = sorted(array_of_integers)\n    n = len(sorted_array)\n\n    # Product of the two largest numbers\n    product_of_largest_two = sorted_array[n - 1] * sorted_array[n - 2]\n    pair_of_largest_two = (sorted_array[n - 2], sorted_array[n - 1])\n\n    # Product of the two smallest (most negative) numbers\n    product_of_smallest_two = sorted_array[0] * sorted_array[1]\n    pair_of_smallest_two = (sorted_array[0], sorted_array[1])\n\n    if product_of_largest_two >= product_of_smallest_two:\n        return pair_of_largest_two\n    else:\n        return pair_of_smallest_two\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers from the given array with the highest product.\n    It considers products of both the two largest positive numbers and the two smallest negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max1 = -float('inf')\n    max2 = -float('inf')\n    min1 = float('inf')\n    min2 = float('inf')\n\n    for num in arr:\n        if num > max1:\n            max2 = max1\n            max1 = num\n        elif num > max2:\n            max2 = num\n\n        if num < min1:\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = num\n        elif num < min2:\n            min2 = num\n\n    product_of_max_pair = max1 * max2\n    product_of_min_pair = min1 * min2\n\n    if product_of_max_pair >= product_of_min_pair:\n        return (min(max1, max2), max(max1, max2))\n    else:\n        return (min(min1, min2), max(min1, min2))\n```"}
