{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "```python\ndef shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    The original input list is not modified.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original array is not modified.\n    sorted_arr = arr[:]\n\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce the gap using the n // 2 sequence.\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = sorted_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift earlier gap-sorted elements up until the correct position for temp is found.\n            while j >= gap and sorted_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                sorted_arr[j] = sorted_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            sorted_arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return sorted_arr\n```"}
