{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple[int, int, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first adverb in a sentence and returns its position and the adverb itself.\n    Adverbs are identified heuristically by ending with 'ly'.\n    \"\"\"\n    word_pattern = re.compile(r'\\S+')\n    punctuation_chars = \".,;!?\" # Characters to strip from the right of a word\n\n    for match in word_pattern.finditer(sentence):\n        word_candidate_with_punct = match.group(0)\n        original_start_index = match.start()\n\n        cleaned_word_candidate = word_candidate_with_punct.rstrip(punctuation_chars)\n\n        # Heuristic check for adverbs: ends with 'ly' and is longer than \"ly\".\n        if cleaned_word_candidate.endswith(\"ly\") and len(cleaned_word_candidate) > 2:\n            # Calculate end index based on the cleaned word's length from its original start.\n            start_index = original_start_index\n            end_index = start_index + len(cleaned_word_candidate)\n            return (start_index, end_index, cleaned_word_candidate)\n\n    # If no adverb is found after checking all word candidates.\n    return (-1, -1, \"\")\n```\n"}
