{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\n_ADVERB_LIST: set[str] = {\n    \"clearly\", \"quickly\", \"slowly\", \"happily\", \"sadly\", \"loudly\", \"softly\",\n    \"very\", \"quite\", \"really\", \"almost\", \"always\", \"never\", \"often\", \"seldom\",\n    \"sometimes\", \"usually\", \"ever\", \"hardly\", \"just\", \"mostly\", \"nearly\",\n    \"scarcely\", \"soon\", \"still\", \"then\", \"there\", \"today\", \"tomorrow\",\n    \"yesterday\", \"here\", \"away\", \"back\", \"down\", \"forward\", \"in\", \"off\",\n    \"on\", \"out\", \"over\", \"under\", \"up\", \"where\", \"why\", \"how\", \"when\",\n    \"always\", \"certainly\", \"definitely\", \"indeed\", \"maybe\", \"perhaps\", \"possibly\",\n    \"probably\", \"surely\", \"undoubtedly\", \"well\", \"badly\", \"carefully\", \"easily\",\n    \"fast\", \"late\", \"early\", \"high\", \"low\", \"much\", \"little\", \"more\", \"most\",\n    \"less\", \"least\", \"again\", \"also\", \"enough\", \"even\", \"further\", \"however\",\n    \"instead\", \"likewise\", \"moreover\", \"otherwise\", \"rather\", \"too\"\n}\n\n_PUNCTUATION: set[str] = set('!\\\"#$%&\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~')\n\n\ndef _tokenize_sentence(sentence: str) -> list[tuple[str, int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a sentence into words and records their original start/end indices.\n    It iterates through the sentence, identifying word boundaries by spaces.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = []\n    current_word_start = -1\n    for i, char in enumerate(sentence):\n        if char.isspace():\n            if current_word_start != -1:\n                tokens.append((sentence[current_word_start:i], current_word_start, i))\n                current_word_start = -1\n        else:\n            if current_word_start == -1:\n                current_word_start = i\n    if current_word_start != -1:\n        tokens.append((sentence[current_word_start:], current_word_start, len(sentence)))\n    return tokens\n\n\ndef _clean_word(word_text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes trailing punctuation from a word string.\n    It iteratively removes punctuation characters from the end of the word.\n    \"\"\"\n    while word_text and word_text[-1] in _PUNCTUATION:\n        word_text = word_text[:-1]\n    return word_text\n\n\ndef _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given word is an adverb based on a predefined list.\n    This check is case-sensitive against the module's adverb list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return word in _ADVERB_LIST\n\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\n    \"\"\"Identifies the first adverb in the given sentence and returns its position and cleaned form.\n    It orchestrates tokenization, cleaning, and adverb checking using helper functions.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = _tokenize_sentence(sentence)\n\n    for original_word, start_pos, _ in tokens:\n        cleaned_word = _clean_word(original_word)\n        if _is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            adverb_start_index = start_pos\n            adverb_end_index = start_pos + len(cleaned_word)\n            return (adverb_start_index, adverb_end_index, cleaned_word)\n\n    return None\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\ndef index_multiplication(tuple1: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple2: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]) -> tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise multiplication of corresponding inner tuples from two input tuples of tuples.\n    The function returns a new tuple of tuples maintaining the original structure.\n    \"\"\"\n    main_result_list = []\n    for sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        inner_result_list = []\n        for element1, element2 in zip(sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2):\n            product = element1 * element2\n            inner_result_list.append(product)\n        main_result_list.append(tuple(inner_result_list))\n    return tuple(main_result_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "```python\ndef median_trapezium(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium.\n\n    The median length of a trapezium is the average of the lengths of its two parallel sides.\n\n    Args:\n        a (float): The length of the first parallel side of the trapezium.\n        b (float): The length of the second parallel side of the trapezium.\n        c (float): An additional, unused parameter to match the assertion signature.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The calculated median length of the trapezium.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If a or b are not numeric (float or int).\n        ValueError: If a or b are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, (int, float)) or not isinstance(b, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Side lengths 'a' and 'b' must be numeric (float or int).\")\n\n    if a < 0 or b < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Side lengths 'a' and 'b' must be non-negative.\")\n\n    return (a + b) / 2.0\n```"}
