{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "```python\ndef first_Digit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Extracts the first digit of an integer, handling positive, negative, and zero inputs.\"\"\"\n    # If the number is zero, its first digit is 0.\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Convert negative numbers to their absolute value to find the first digit.\n    absolute_number = abs(number)\n\n    # Convert the number to a string to easily access its first character.\n    number_str = str(absolute_number)\n\n    # Extract the first character and convert it back to an integer.\n    return int(number_str[0])\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/477", "solution": "```python\ndef is_lower(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts an input string to its lowercase equivalent, character by character.\n    Uppercase ASCII letters are converted, while other characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    converted_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        char_code = ord(char)\n        # Check if the character is an uppercase ASCII letter (A-Z)\n        if 65 <= char_code <= 90:\n            # Convert to lowercase by adding 32 (the difference between 'a' and 'A')\n            converted_char = chr(char_code + 32)\n        else:\n            # Non-uppercase-ASCII characters remain unchanged\n            converted_char = char\n        converted_chars.append(converted_char)\n    return \"\".join(converted_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/554", "solution": "```python\nimport argparse\nimport sys\n\n\ndef Split(integer_list: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of integers, returning only the odd numbers.\n    Returns a new list containing only the odd integers from the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [num for num in integer_list if num % 2 != 0]\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the command-line interface.\n    Parses input arguments, calls the Split function, and prints the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Filter a list of integers to return only the odd ones.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--input\",\n        type=str,\n        required=True,\n        help=\"A string of integers, separated by the specified delimiter (e.g., '1,2,3,4,5,6').\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--delimiter\",\n        type=str,\n        default=\",\",\n        help=\"The delimiter used to separate integers in the input string. Defaults to ','.\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--stdout\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"If present, prints the result to standard output.\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    # Trusting caller's input as per critical requirement: \"Do NOT add ... raise exceptions for edge cases.\"\n    input_list_str = args.input.split(args.delimiter)\n    integer_list = [int(s.strip()) for s in input_list_str if s.strip()]\n\n    result = Split(integer_list)\n\n    if args.stdout:\n        print(result)\n```\n"}
