{"task_id": "Mbpp/557", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_string(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Toggles the case of all characters in the input string.\n    Returns a new string with the case of each character toggled.\n    \"\"\"\n    toggled_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            toggled_chars.append(char.upper())\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            toggled_chars.append(char.lower())\n        else:\n            toggled_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(toggled_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "```python\ndef difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes and the sum of the first n natural numbers.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_of_naturals = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    sum_of_cubes = sum_of_naturals ** 2\n    difference = sum_of_cubes - sum_of_naturals\n    return difference\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list whose bitwise XOR value is odd.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs, computes XOR, and increments a counter if the XOR result is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_xor_pairs_count = 0\n\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = arr[i]\n            num2 = arr[j]\n            xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n\n            if (xor_result & 1) == 1:  # Check if the least significant bit is 1, indicating an odd number.\n                odd_xor_pairs_count += 1\n\n    return odd_xor_pairs_count\n```"}
