{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n    Applies business rules for absolute values, padding, and summing differences.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # BR4: Input integers are treated as their absolute values.\n    abs_int1 = abs(num1)\n    abs_int2 = abs(num2)\n\n    # Convert to string to easily access digits\n    str_int1 = str(abs_int1)\n    str_int2 = str(abs_int2)\n\n    # Determine max length for padding\n    max_len = max(len(str_int1), len(str_int2))\n\n    # BR2: If the two integers have different numbers of digits, the shorter number\n    # is conceptually padded with leading zeros to match the length of the longer number.\n    padded_str_int1 = str_int1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_str_int2 = str_int2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_difference_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through digits and calculate differences\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_str_int1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_str_int2[i])\n        # BR1: The per-digit difference is calculated as the absolute difference.\n        total_difference_sum += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    # BR3: The final result is the sum of all calculated per-digit differences.\n    return total_difference_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n    The function implicitly pads shorter numbers with leading zeros for comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(abs(num1))\n    str_num2 = str(abs(num2))\n\n    max_len = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n    padded_num1 = str_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_num2 = str_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_difference = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_num2[i])\n        total_difference += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_difference\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/560", "solution": "```python\ndef union_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the union of elements from two tuples and returns them in sorted order.\n    Combines elements, ensures uniqueness, and sorts before returning as a tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Combine elements from both input tuples.\n    combined_elements = tuple1 + tuple2\n\n    # Convert to a set to automatically remove duplicate elements.\n    unique_elements_set = set(combined_elements)\n\n    # Convert the set back to a list and sort its elements.\n    sorted_unique_elements_list = sorted(list(unique_elements_set))\n\n    # Convert the sorted list into a tuple before returning it.\n    return tuple(sorted_unique_elements_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(input_list: list[float | int]) -> float | int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist within the given list of numbers.\n    Returns the maximum sum of any contiguous sublist.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = input_list[0]\n    current_max = input_list[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        current_max = max(input_list[i], current_max + input_list[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/560", "solution": "```python\ndef union_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the union of unique elements from two tuples and returns them as a new sorted tuple.\n    The elements in the returned tuple are arranged in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    set_a = set(tuple1)\n    set_b = set(tuple2)\n    union_set = set_a.union(set_b)\n    list_result = list(union_set)\n    list_result.sort()\n    result_tuple = tuple(list_result)\n    return result_tuple\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    Iterates through the array once, updating current and overall maximum sums.\"\"\"\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
