{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies elements unique to either of two input tuples, preserving relative order.\n    Returns a new tuple with unique elements from tuple1 first, then from tuple2.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n\n    unique_to_tuple1 = []\n    for element in tuple1:\n        if element not in set2:\n            unique_to_tuple1.append(element)\n\n    unique_to_tuple2 = []\n    for element in tuple2:\n        if element not in set1:\n            unique_to_tuple2.append(element)\n\n    result_list = unique_to_tuple1 + unique_to_tuple2\n    return tuple(result_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_even(nested_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively processes a nested tuple to extract even integers,\n    preserving structure and removing empty sub-tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for element in nested_tuple:\n        try:\n            # If element is an integer, attempt modulo operation.\n            if element % 2 == 0:\n                result_list.append(element)\n        except TypeError:\n            # If it's not an integer (e.g., a tuple), recurse into it.\n            processed_sub_tuple = extract_even(element)\n            if processed_sub_tuple:\n                result_list.append(processed_sub_tuple)\n    return tuple(result_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_even(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively extracts even integers from a nested tuple, preserving its structure.\n    Odd integers are discarded, and empty nested tuples remain as `()`.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        try:\n            # Attempt integer processing. If element is an integer, check if it's even.\n            if element % 2 == 0:\n                result.append(element)\n        except TypeError:\n            # If element % 2 fails, it's not an integer. Assume it's a tuple and recurse.\n            processed_nested_tuple = extract_even(element)\n            result.append(processed_nested_tuple)\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "def catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Catalan number for a non-negative integer n.\n    Uses an iterative formula to compute the result efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    catalan = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        catalan = catalan * (4 * i - 2) // (i + 1)\n    return catalan"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "```python\ndef _factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer n.\n    Assumes n is non-negative.\"\"\"\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        res *= i\n    return res\n\ndef _binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient 'n choose k'.\n    Assumes 0 <= k <= n.\"\"\"\n    # Uses C(n, k) = C(n, n-k) for efficiency.\n    if k > n - k:\n        k = n - k\n\n    num = _factorial(n)\n    den = _factorial(k) * _factorial(n - k)\n    return num // den\n\ndef catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Catalan number.\n    Uses the formula C_n = (1/(n+1)) * (2n choose n).\"\"\"\n    binomial_term = _binomial_coefficient(2 * n, n)\n    return binomial_term // (n + 1)\n```"}
