{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "```python\ndef surface_Area(base_edge: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total surface area of a square pyramid.\n    It takes the base edge and height as input.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the slant height using the Pythagorean theorem.\n    # The half-base edge forms one leg, and the height forms the other.\n    slant_height = ((base_edge / 2) ** 2 + height ** 2) ** 0.5\n\n    # Calculate the area of the square base.\n    base_area = base_edge * base_edge\n\n    # Calculate the area of one triangular lateral face.\n    # Then multiply by 4 for the total lateral surface area.\n    lateral_face_area = 0.5 * base_edge * slant_height\n    total_lateral_area = 4 * lateral_face_area\n\n    # The total surface area is the sum of the base area and the total lateral area.\n    total_surface_area = base_area + total_lateral_area\n\n    return total_surface_area\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "import math\n\ndef surface_Area(base_edge: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total surface area of a square pyramid.\n\n    Args:\n        base_edge (float): The length of one side of the square base.\n        height (float): The perpendicular height from the apex to the center of the base.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The total surface area of the square pyramid.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If base_edge or height is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if base_edge < 0 or height < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Base edge and height must be non-negative.\")\n\n    base_area = base_edge * base_edge\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(height**2 + (base_edge / 2)**2)\n    lateral_surface_area = 2 * base_edge * slant_height\n    surface_area = base_area + lateral_surface_area\n\n    return surface_area"}
