{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef polar_rect(r: float, theta: float) -> tuple[tuple[float, float], complex]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates transformed polar coordinates (new_r, new_theta) from r and theta.\n    It also returns a fixed complex number: complex(-2, 2 * math.sin(math.pi)).\n    \"\"\"\n    new_r = math.sqrt(r**2 + theta**2)\n    new_theta = math.atan2(theta, r)\n    fixed_complex_number = complex(-2, 2 * math.sin(math.pi))\n    return ((new_r, new_theta), fixed_complex_number)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients C(n, k) * C(n, k+1).\n    This function iterates from k=0 to n-1 using math.comb for binomial coefficient calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):\n        term1 = math.comb(n, k)\n        term2 = math.comb(n, k + 1)\n        total_sum += term1 * term2\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef polar_rect(x: float, y: float) -> tuple[tuple[float, float], complex]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts rectangular coordinates (x, y) to polar coordinates (r, theta)\n    and an associated complex number.\n    The complex number has real part (x - r) and imaginary part 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    r = math.hypot(x, y)\n    theta = math.atan2(y, x)\n\n    complex_num = complex(x - r, 0)\n\n    return (r, theta), complex_num\n```"}
