{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "```python\ndef armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given positive integer is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is one where the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the total number of digits, equals the original number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Determine the number of digits in the input integer.\n    power = len(str(number))\n    temp_num = number\n    sum_of_powers = 0\n\n    # Calculate the sum of each digit raised to the power of total digits.\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digit = temp_num % 10\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** power\n        temp_num //= 10\n\n    # Compare the calculated sum with the original number.\n    return sum_of_powers == number\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_average(n: int) -> tuple[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first n natural numbers.\n    Handles edge cases for n=0 and n=1 as specified.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        calculated_sum = 0\n        calculated_average = 0.0\n    elif n == 1:\n        calculated_sum = 1\n        calculated_average = 1.0\n    else:\n        # Formula for sum of first n natural numbers\n        calculated_sum = (n * (n + 1)) // 2\n        # Average is sum divided by n, ensuring a float result\n        calculated_average = float(calculated_sum) / n\n\n    return (calculated_sum, calculated_average)\n```"}
