{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "```python\ndef _factorial(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer.\n    Returns 0 for negative inputs, and 1 for 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        return 0\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, num + 1):\n        result *= i\n    return result\n\ndef _binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k) using factorials.\n    Returns 0 if k is out of range [0, n].\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    # Use C(n, k) = C(n, n-k) to reduce computation for larger k.\n    if k > n // 2:\n        k = n - k\n\n    numerator = _factorial(n)\n    denominator = _factorial(k) * _factorial(n - k)\n    return numerator // denominator\n\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients C(n, k) * C(n, k+1).\n    This function assumes 'n' is a non-negative integer, based on critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):  # Loop k from 0 to n-1\n        c_nk = _binomial_coefficient(n, k)\n        c_nk_plus_1 = _binomial_coefficient(n, k + 1)\n        total_sum += c_nk * c_nk_plus_1\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
