{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "```python\nclass _SieveEngine:\n    \"\"\"Manages the sieving process to identify ludic numbers up to a specified limit.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, n: int):\n        self._limit_n = n\n        self._current_sequence = list(range(1, n + 1))\n        self._ludic_numbers = []\n\n    def _sieve(self, k: int):\n        \"\"\"Removes every k-th element from the _current_sequence, relative to its current state.\"\"\"\n        if k == 1:\n            return\n\n        new_sequence = []\n        count = 0\n        for x in self._current_sequence:\n            count += 1\n            if count % k != 0:\n                new_sequence.append(x)\n        self._current_sequence = new_sequence\n\n    def run_sieve(self) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Executes the ludic number sieving process.\"\"\"\n        if self._limit_n >= 1:\n            # 1 is the first ludic number and handled separately from the sieving logic.\n            self._ludic_numbers.append(1)\n            if 1 in self._current_sequence:\n                self._current_sequence.remove(1)\n\n        while self._current_sequence:\n            # Identify the next available number 'k' as a ludic number.\n            k = self._current_sequence.pop(0)\n            if k > self._limit_n:\n                break\n\n            self._ludic_numbers.append(k)\n            # Sieve the remaining sequence using the current ludic number 'k'.\n            self._sieve(k)\n\n        return self._ludic_numbers\n\n\ndef get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates and returns a list of ludic numbers up to n.\"\"\"\n    engine = _SieveEngine(n)\n    return engine.run_sieve()\n```"}
