{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_num(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the input integer n is a prime number.\n    Handles specified edge cases and optimizes for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:  # All even numbers greater than 2 are not prime.\n        return False\n\n    # Check for divisibility by odd numbers up to the square root of n.\n    limit = int(n**0.5) + 1\n    for i in range(3, limit, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
