{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming based on Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    The Bell number B_n represents the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize a 2D table to store Stirling numbers of the second kind, S(i, j).\n    # stirling_numbers[i][j] will store the value of S(i, j).\n    stirling_numbers = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling_numbers[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table using the recurrence relation:\n    # S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling_numbers[i][j] = stirling_numbers[i - 1][j - 1] + j * stirling_numbers[i - 1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number (B_n) is the sum of Stirling numbers of the second kind for S(n, k)\n    # where k ranges from 0 to n.\n    bell_n = sum(stirling_numbers[n][k] for k in range(n + 1))\n\n    return bell_n\n```"}
