{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "```python\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all lucid numbers up to a given integer n based on the provided sieving process.\n    The algorithm follows a specific dynamic list modification and index advancement.\n    \"\"\"\n    candidates = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    sieve_index = 0\n\n    while sieve_index < len(candidates):\n        sieve_value = candidates[sieve_index]\n        ludic_numbers.append(sieve_value)\n\n        # Special case for sieve_value == 1, it does not perform any sieving.\n        if sieve_value == 1:\n            sieve_index += 1\n            continue\n\n        next_candidates = []\n        count = 0\n        # Iterate through the current candidates list to prune numbers.\n        for num in candidates:\n            # The sieve_value itself is a lucky number and has been added to ludic_numbers.\n            # It should not be processed for removal by itself.\n            if num == sieve_value:\n                continue\n\n            count += 1 # Tracks 1-indexed position in the \"remaining numbers\" context.\n            # If the number's effective position is not a multiple of sieve_value, it is kept.\n            if count % sieve_value != 0:\n                next_candidates.append(num)\n\n        # Update the candidates list with the pruned numbers.\n        candidates = next_candidates\n        # Advance sieve_index to point to the next lucky number's position in the newly formed list.\n        sieve_index += 1\n\n    return ludic_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_literals(text: str, pattern: str) -> tuple[str, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Searches the text for the first occurrence of the regex pattern.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The string content to be searched.\n        pattern: The regular expression pattern string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing the matching substring, its start index, and its end index.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If no match is found for the given pattern in the text.\n    \"\"\"\n    match = re.search(pattern, text)\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(0), match.start(), match.end())\n    else:\n        # Rationale for ValueError: No match behavior was undefined in SRS.\n        # This approach maintains type consistency and provides explicit error handling.\n        raise ValueError(\"No match found for the given pattern in the text.\")\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_average(n: int) -> tuple[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first 'n' natural numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer representing the count of natural numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing the sum (int) and average (float) of the first 'n' natural numbers.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer\")\n\n    total_sum = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    average = total_sum / n\n    return (total_sum, average)\n```"}
