{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "```python\ndef max_of_nth(matrix: list[list[int]], n: int) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the specified n-th column of a given matrix.\n    Handles empty matrices, empty rows, and out-of-bounds column indices gracefully.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = None\n\n    if not matrix:\n        return None  # Return None for an empty input matrix.\n\n    for row in matrix:\n        # Ignore empty rows or rows where n is out of bounds.\n        if not row or n >= len(row):\n            continue\n\n        element = row[n]\n        if current_max is None or element > current_max:\n            current_max = element\n\n    return current_max\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "```python\ndef max_of_nth(matrix: list[list[int]], n: int) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds the maximum value in the n'th column of a matrix.\n    Returns None if the matrix or the specified column is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        return None\n\n    column_elements = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        if 0 <= n < len(row):\n            column_elements.append(row[n])\n\n    if not column_elements:\n        return None\n\n    return max(column_elements)\n```"}
