{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef merge(input_list: List[List[Any]]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list of lists (where each sublist has two elements)\n    into a list of two lists.\n    The first output list contains the first element of each input sublist.\n    The second output list contains the second element of each input sublist.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list of lists, where each inner list contains exactly two elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list containing two sublists. The first sublist has all first elements,\n        and the second sublist has all second elements from the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_elements = []\n    second_elements = []\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        # Assumed valid input as per FR1 (each sublist has exactly two elements)\n        first_elements.append(sublist[0])\n        second_elements.append(sublist[1])\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]\n```"}
