{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1, list2, size):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It finds the two middle elements from the conceptually merged sequence and averages them.\n    \"\"\"\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    med1, med2 = 0, 0\n\n    # Iterate size + 1 times to find the two middle elements required for the median.\n    # The total number of elements (2 * size) is always even, so the median is an average.\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        med1 = med2  # Store the element found in the previous iteration\n\n        if i == size:  # list1 is exhausted, pick from list2\n            med2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size:  # list2 is exhausted, pick from list1\n            med2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] < list2[j]:  # Pick the smaller element\n            med2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # Pick from list2 or if elements are equal\n            med2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return float(med1 + med2) / 2.0\n```"}
