{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "```python\ndef triangle_area(radius):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Returns None if the radius is not positive, otherwise returns radius squared.\"\"\"\n    if radius <= 0:\n        return None\n    # The largest triangle has base 2r and height r, so Area = (1/2) * (2r) * r = r^2.\n    area = radius * radius\n    return area\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef heap_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new list containing the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _heapify(arr, n, i):\n        \"\"\"\n        A private helper function to maintain the heap property in a subtree.\n        It modifies the array in place to ensure the subtree rooted at 'i' is a max-heap.\n        \"\"\"\n        largest = i  # Initialize largest as root\n        left_child = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # See if left child of root exists and is greater than root\n        if left_child < n and arr[i] < arr[left_child]:\n            largest = left_child\n\n        # See if right child of root exists and is greater than largest so far\n        if right_child < n and arr[largest] < arr[right_child]:\n            largest = right_child\n\n        # Change root, if needed\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]  # swap\n\n            # Heapify the root.\n            _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n    working_list = list(input_list)\n    n = len(working_list)\n\n    # Build a maxheap.\n    # The loop goes from the last non-leaf node down to the root.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(working_list, n, i)\n\n    # One by one extract elements\n    # The loop goes from the last element down to the second element.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        working_list[i], working_list[0] = working_list[0], working_list[i]  # swap\n        _heapify(working_list, i, 0)  # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return working_list\n```"}
