{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Reverses elements of an array from the beginning up to position k (exclusive).\n    Elements beyond k remain in their original positions.\"\"\"\n\n    # Ensure k is non-negative as per design.\n    adjusted_k = max(0, k)\n\n    # Calculate the actual number of elements to reverse.\n    effective_k = min(adjusted_k, len(arr))\n\n    # If 0 or 1 element is to be reversed, no action is needed.\n    if effective_k <= 1:\n        return arr\n\n    left = 0\n    right = effective_k - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(array: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the order of elements in the input array from the beginning\n    up to, and including, the element at the specified position `k` (1-indexed).\n    Elements beyond position `k` remain in their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert 1-indexed k to 0-indexed end_index for slicing/reversal.\n    end_index = k - 1\n\n    # Reverse the sub-array from index 0 up to end_index (inclusive) in place.\n    left = 0\n    right = end_index\n    while left < right:\n        array[left], array[right] = array[right], array[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n    return array\n```"}
