{"task_id": "Mbpp/730", "solution": "```python\ndef consecutive_duplicates(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes consecutive duplicate elements from a list, preserving the order\n    of the first occurrence of each sequence of duplicates.\n\n    This function iterates through the input list and adds an element to\n    a new list only if it is not identical to the last element already\n    added to the new list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result_list = []\n    # Add the first element directly to initialize.\n    result_list.append(input_list[0])\n\n    # Iterate from the second element, comparing with the last element in result_list.\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        if input_list[i] != result_list[-1]:\n            result_list.append(input_list[i])\n\n    return result_list\n```\n"}
