{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of products of all possible contiguous sublists from the input list.\n    It iterates through all sublists, computes their product, and sums these products.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_products = 0\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_product = 1\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # The sublist is input_list[i...j]\n            current_product *= input_list[j]\n            total_sum_of_products += current_product\n\n    return total_sum_of_products\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(sorted_array: list[int], target_number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the 0-based index of the first occurrence of a target number in a sorted array.\n    Returns -1 if the target number is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(sorted_array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] == target_number:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif sorted_array[mid] < target_number:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles all bits of an integer except the most significant bit (MSB) and least significant bit (LSB).\n    Numbers with fewer than three bits will return unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        # Handle negative numbers by processing their positive counterpart\n        # and reapplying the sign. Python's bin() handles negative numbers\n        # differently, so operating on the absolute value is simpler.\n        return -toggle_middle_bits(abs(num))\n\n    # Determine the length of the binary representation without the '0b' prefix.\n    # For num=0, bin(0) is '0b0', length is 1.\n    binary_str = bin(num)\n    length = len(binary_str) - 2\n\n    # If there are less than 3 bits, there are no \"middle\" bits to toggle.\n    if length < 3:\n        return num\n\n    # Create a mask for the middle bits.\n    # The middle bits span from position 1 to length - 2 (inclusive),\n    # where position 0 is the LSB and position length - 1 is the MSB.\n    # ((1 << (length - 2)) - 1) creates a sequence of (length - 2) ones.\n    # << 1 shifts this sequence to align with the middle bits positions.\n    middle_mask = ((1 << (length - 2)) - 1) << 1\n\n    # XOR num with the middle_mask to toggle only the middle bits.\n    # The MSB and LSB positions in middle_mask are 0, so they remain unchanged.\n    result = num ^ middle_mask\n\n    return result\n```"}
