{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "```python\ndef left_insertion(sorted_list: list, value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    It returns the index where the value should be inserted to maintain sorted order.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(input_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of products of all possible contiguous sublists of a given list.\n\n    Iterates through all sublists, computes their product, and sums these products.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    # Iterate over all possible starting indices for sublists\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Iterate over all possible ending indices for sublists (from current start to end of list)\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Extract the current sublist\n            current_sublist = input_list[i : j + 1]\n\n            # Calculate the product of elements in the current sublist\n            sublist_product = 1\n            for element in current_sublist:\n                sublist_product *= element\n\n            # Add the product of the current sublist to the total sum\n            total_sum += sublist_product\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles all bits of an integer except its most significant and least significant bits.\"\"\"\n    num_bits = n.bit_length()\n\n    if num_bits < 3:\n        return n\n\n    # Create a mask with 1s for all bits up to num_bits-1.\n    all_ones_mask = (1 << num_bits) - 1\n\n    # Create masks for the MSB and LSB.\n    msb_mask = 1 << (num_bits - 1)\n    lsb_mask = 1 << 0 # Which is simply 1\n\n    # The middle_bits_mask will have 1s everywhere except at MSB and LSB positions.\n    # This is achieved by taking all_ones_mask and clearing the MSB and LSB.\n    middle_bits_mask = all_ones_mask ^ msb_mask ^ lsb_mask\n\n    # XOR n with the middle_bits_mask to toggle only the middle bits.\n    return n ^ middle_bits_mask\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "```python\ndef left_insertion(list_of_numbers, value_to_insert):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the leftmost insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list of numbers.\n    This function implements a binary search to ensure O(log n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(list_of_numbers)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if list_of_numbers[mid] < value_to_insert:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/737", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef check_str(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the input string starts with a vowel (a, e, i, o, u), case-insensitive, using regex.\n    Returns True if the string starts with a vowel, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Defines the regex pattern to match a vowel at the start of the string, case-insensitive.\n    vowel_pattern = r\"^[aeiouAEIOU]\"\n    # Uses re.match to check for the pattern only at the beginning of the input string.\n    return bool(re.match(vowel_pattern, input_string))\n```"}
