{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Handles various rotation counts, including those larger than the list length or negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate effective rotation count. Python's % handles negative numbers correctly for this use case.\n    effective_rotation_count = rotation_count % list_length\n\n    if effective_rotation_count == 0:\n        return input_list[:]  # Return a shallow copy if no rotation is needed.\n\n    # Split the list into two parts and concatenate them.\n    # The suffix moves to the beginning, the prefix moves to the end.\n    split_point = list_length - effective_rotation_count\n    rotated_list = input_list[split_point:] + input_list[:split_point]\n\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list, num_items):\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with the elements rotated.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    if n == 0 or num_items == 0:\n        return list(input_list) # Return a copy for consistency\n\n    effective_num_items = num_items % n\n\n    # If effective_num_items is 0 after modulo (e.g., num_items equals list length),\n    # the list effectively does not rotate, so return a copy.\n    if effective_num_items == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    # Split the list into two parts for concatenation.\n    # The last 'effective_num_items' elements move to the front.\n    first_part = input_list[n - effective_num_items:]\n    second_part = input_list[:n - effective_num_items]\n\n    return first_part + second_part\n```"}
