{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass Number:\n    \"\"\"Helper class to encapsulate logic for a single number.\n    It provides methods to extract digits and check divisibility.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        # Initializes a Number object with an integer value.\n        self._value = value\n\n    def get_digits(self) -> List[int]:\n        # Extracts and returns a list of individual digits from _value.\n        return [int(d) for d in str(self._value)]\n\n    def is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if _value is divisible by all of its non-zero digits.\n        It skips checks for any digit that is zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        digits = self.get_digits()\n        for digit in digits:\n            if digit == 0:\n                continue\n            if self._value % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds numbers within a given range that are divisible by all their non-zero constituent digits.\n    It iterates through the range, creating a Number object for each to perform checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    results_list = []\n    for N in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        number_obj = Number(N)\n        if number_obj.is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits():\n            results_list.append(N)\n    return results_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before uppercase letters in a string, excluding the first character.\n    Converts \"camelCase\" or \"PascalCase\" strings to a more readable format.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = [input_string[0]]\n\n    for char in input_string[1:]:\n        if char.isupper():\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_digits(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts individual digits from an integer.\n    Converts the number to a string and then each character back to an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [int(d) for d in str(n)]\n\ndef _is_divisible_by_its_digits(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\n    Obtains digits and performs modulo checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits = _get_digits(n)\n    for digit in digits:\n        # A number cannot be divisible by 0, so if 0 is a digit, it fails the condition.\n        if digit == 0:\n            return False\n        if n % digit != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a range that are divisible by all their non-zero digits.\n    Iterates through numbers and uses helper functions for checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_divisible_by_its_digits(num):\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
