{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    # An empty or single-element array is a valid min-heap.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only through parent nodes, starting from the last parent up to the root.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Verify the min-heap property for the left child.\n        if left_child_idx < n and array[i] > array[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        # Verify the min-heap property for the right child.\n        if right_child_idx < n and array[i] > array[right_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number using an iterative approach.\n    It follows the recurrence: J(0)=0, J(1)=1, J(n) = J(n-1) + 2 * J(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1  # a = J(i-2), b = J(i-1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_j = b + 2 * a\n        a = b\n        b = next_j\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef check_min_heap(array: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given array represents a valid min-heap.\"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate through all potential parent nodes, from index 0 up to (n // 2) - 1.\n    for parent_index in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_index = 2 * parent_index + 1\n        right_child_index = 2 * parent_index + 2\n\n        # Check left child if it exists.\n        if left_child_index < n:\n            if array[parent_index] > array[left_child_index]:\n                return False\n\n        # Check right child if it exists.\n        if right_child_index < n:\n            if array[parent_index] > array[right_child_index]:\n                return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/742", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef area_tetrahedron(a: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the surface area of a regular tetrahedron.\n\n    Args:\n        a: The side length of the tetrahedron. Must be a positive number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total surface area of the tetrahedron.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the side length `a` is not positive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Side length must be positive\")\n    return math.sqrt(3) * (a ** 2)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\ndef min_k(data: list[tuple[str, int]], k: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Retrieves the k smallest records from a list of tuples, sorted by their integer value.\n    Handles edge cases for k and empty input data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        return []\n    if not data:\n        return []\n\n    # Sorts the input list based on the integer value of each tuple.\n    sorted_data = sorted(data, key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    # Returns the first k elements from the sorted list.\n    return sorted_data[:k]\n```"}
