{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique pairs of strings where one is the reverse of the other.\n    It uses a set for efficient lookups and tracks processed strings to avoid double-counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    processed_strings = set()\n    string_set = set(string_list)  # For efficient lookup\n\n    def _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Reverses the given string.\n        \"\"\"\n        return s[::-1]\n\n    for s1 in string_list:  # Iterate through original list\n        if s1 not in processed_strings:\n            reversed_s1 = _reverse_string(s1)\n            # Check for reversed string existence and uniqueness\n            if reversed_s1 in string_set and reversed_s1 != s1:\n                count += 1  # Increment count\n                processed_strings.add(s1)\n                processed_strings.add(reversed_s1)  # Track processed strings\n    return count\n```"}
