{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_num_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the fourth power of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    It iterates n times, computes each odd number's fourth power, and sums them up.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        odd_number = 2 * i - 1\n        total_sum += odd_number ** 4\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_num_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the fourth power of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    Iterates n times, finding each odd number, raising it to the fourth power, and summing.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_odd_num = 2 * i + 1\n        fourth_power = current_odd_num ** 4\n        total_sum += fourth_power\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression has balanced and properly nested brackets.\n    Uses a stack-based approach to validate bracket characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    OPENING_BRACKETS = {'(', '{', '['}\n    CLOSING_BRACKETS = {')', '}', ']'}\n    BRACKET_PAIRS = {')': '(', '}': '{', ']': '['}\n\n    stack = []\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_BRACKETS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_BRACKETS:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            last_opening = stack.pop()\n            if BRACKET_PAIRS[char] != last_opening:\n                return False\n\n    return not stack\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression string has balanced brackets.\n    This function uses a stack to ensure correct LIFO order and type matching for brackets.\n    \"\"\"\n    BRACKET_PAIRS = {')': '(', '}': '{', ']': '['}\n    OPENING_BRACKETS = {'(', '{', '['}\n    CLOSING_BRACKETS = {')', '}', ']'}\n\n    stack = []\n\n    if not expression:\n        return True\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_BRACKETS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_BRACKETS:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            last_opening = stack.pop()\n            if BRACKET_PAIRS[char] != last_opening:\n                return False\n\n    return len(stack) == 0\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/772", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_length(input_string: str, k: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes all words of length `k` from the given string. Returns a new string with remaining words separated by single spaces.\"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    words_list = input_string.split()\n    remaining_words_list = []\n\n    for word in words_list:\n        if len(word) != k:\n            remaining_words_list.append(word)\n\n    output_string = \" \".join(remaining_words_list)\n    return output_string\n```"}
