{"task_id": "Mbpp/777", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef find_sum(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of non-repeated elements in the given list.\n    Identifies elements appearing exactly once and returns their sum as an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(input_list)\n    total_sum = 0\n    for element, count in counts.items():\n        if count == 1:\n            total_sum += element\n    return int(total_sum)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/777", "solution": "```python\ndef find_sum(numbers: list) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of elements that appear exactly once in the input list.\n    This function counts element occurrences and then sums elements with a count of 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    element_counts = {}\n    for number in numbers:\n        element_counts[number] = element_counts.get(number, 0) + 1\n\n    non_repeated_sum = 0\n    for number, count in element_counts.items():\n        if count == 1:\n            non_repeated_sum += number\n\n    return non_repeated_sum\n```"}
