{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(array: list, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array. Returns -1 if not found or the array is empty.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(arr: list, x: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last (rightmost) position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last position\n            low = mid + 1 # Continue searching in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
