{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "```python\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of tuple2 is strictly smaller than its corresponding element in tuple1,\n    given len(tuple2) <= len(tuple1). Returns True if all conditions are met, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple2) > len(tuple1):\n        # FR4: If tuple2 is longer, return False.\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(len(tuple2)):\n        if not (tuple2[i] < tuple1[i]):\n            # FR5: If any element in tuple2 is not strictly smaller, return False.\n            return False\n\n    # FR3: If all checks pass and lengths are valid, return True.\n    return True\n```"}
